SDL2: never resize a fullscreen window on guest mode changes.

A fullscreen window already scales the guest through
SDL_RenderSetLogicalSize, so resizing it on every guest mode change only
makes the kmsdrm backend rebuild its scanout surfaces for nothing.

--- ./ui/sdl2.c
+++ ./ui/sdl2.c
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@
 
 void sdl2_window_resize(struct sdl2_console *scon)
 {
-    if (!scon->real_window) {
+    if (!scon->real_window || gui_fullscreen) {
         return;
     }
 
